summary:
  The artist's name is put into the search address with encodeURI, which
  leaves & = ? # + / standing, so a name can end the query, add a second
  one or change the path it is searched under.

history:
  The links for the artist on air are a fixed host and path with the name
  as one query value. The name comes out of a stream's title line, which
  the station writes: "Earth, Wind & Fire" would search for "Earth, Wind",
  "A+B" for "A B", and a title built for it could hand the site any other
  parameter. MusicLinks escapes the name as a single value. This mutant
  escapes it as if it were a whole address.

target:
  package/contents/ui/MusicLinks.js

find:
      return encodeURIComponent(who).replace(/[!'()*]/g, function(ch) {

replace:
      return encodeURI(who).replace(/[!'()*]/g, function(ch) {

expect:
  Killed by tests/qml/tst_musiclinks.qml::test_a_name_goes_into_the_address_as_one_value.
  Line-neutral.
